/// @file gba/codec
/// @brief Compile-time-first, byte-oriented codec framework for GBA.
///
/// Inspired by the Muesli codec library:
/// https://github.com/felixjones/muesli
///
/// `gba::codec` describes wire formats as small, composable constexpr values
/// ("codecs-as-values") instead of runtime schema descriptions. Composite
/// codecs are not necessarily structural C++ values; link APIs accept a
/// namespace-scope constexpr codec through a reference template parameter.
/// Every codec exposes `value_type` and can manufacture a decoder/encoder pair:
///
/// - A decoder is driven one byte at a time: `feed(std::byte) -> step`, where
///   `step` is `more` (need another byte), `done` (`value()` is now valid),
///   or `error` (the input seen so far is malformed).
/// - An encoder is a pull source: `next() -> std::optional<std::byte>`,
///   returning `std::nullopt` once fully emitted.
///
/// This byte-at-a-time contract means codecs work equally well fed from a
/// whole buffer (`gba::codec::decode`/`encode`), a link-cable byte stream, or
/// any other incremental source, without change. Malformed input is always
/// reported through `gba::codec::error` (via `gba::codec::result<T>`, an
/// alias of `std::expected`); nothing in this module throws.
///
/// Fixed-size codecs (`FixedSizeCodec`, exposing `encoded_size`) never
/// allocate. Only the dynamic container codecs (`vector_of`, `string_codec`)
/// are permitted to allocate, since their wire size is inherently unbounded.
///
/// ## Basic usage
///
/// @code{.cpp}
/// #include <gba/codec>
///
/// constexpr auto codec = gba::codec::uint32_codec;
/// std::array<std::byte, 4> buffer{};
/// gba::codec::encode(codec, 0xDEADBEEFu, buffer);
/// const auto outcome = gba::codec::decode(codec, buffer);
/// // outcome.value == gba::codec::result<std::uint32_t>{0xDEADBEEFu}
/// @endcode
///
/// ## Aggregate projection
///
/// @code{.cpp}
/// struct point { std::int32_t x, y; };
///
/// constexpr auto point_codec = gba::codec::make_tuple_codec(
///     gba::codec::member<&point::x>(gba::codec::int32_codec),
///     gba::codec::member<&point::y>(gba::codec::int32_codec)
/// ).apply<point>();
/// @endcode
///
/// ## Variable-length values
///
/// @code{.cpp}
/// // A varint-encoded array length, then that many elements.
/// constexpr auto ids_codec = gba::codec::vector_of(gba::codec::unsigned_varint_codec);
/// @endcode
